\begin_layout Itemize
It may not be obvious,
 but we can think of an application of 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbf{X}$
\end_inset

 as a 180-degree rotation about the 
\begin_inset Formula $\hat{x}$
\end_inset

 axis in the Bloch sphere.
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
We can make an arbitrary rotation through angle 
\begin_inset Formula $\theta_{x}$
\end_inset

 about 
\begin_inset Formula $\hat{x}$
\end_inset

 by forming the 
\begin_inset Formula $x$
\end_inset

-rotation operator from an exponential of 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbf{X}$
\end_inset

:
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{equation}
\mathbf{R}_{x}\left(\theta_{x}\right)=\exp\left(-i\frac{\theta_{x}}{2}\mathbf{X}\right)=\begin{bmatrix}\cos\left(\theta_{x}/2\right) & -i\sin\left(\theta_{x}/2\right)\\
-i\sin\left(\theta_{x}/2\right) & \cos\left(\theta_{x}/2\right)
\end{bmatrix}.\label{eq:ArbitraryXRotation}
\end{equation}

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
We add a function for an arbitrary rotation 
\begin_inset Formula $\theta_{x}$
\end_inset

 about 
\begin_inset Formula $\hat{x}$
\end_inset

 to our file
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
Similarly,
 an application of 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbf{Z}$
\end_inset

 is a 180-degree rotation about the 
\begin_inset Formula $\hat{z}$
\end_inset

 axis in the Bloch sphere,
 and
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Itemize
We can form an application of 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbf{Y}$
\end_inset

 is a 180-degree rotation about the 
\begin_inset Formula $\hat{y}$
\end_inset

 axis in the Bloch sphere
\end_layout

